/-! # Stage H3b: cellular homology and the rank-twelve projector on the lifted complex (FROZEN SPEC)

The frozen spec for `docs/briefs/cloud-spec-h3b.md` (`docs/specs/PrymParabolicRealization.md`).
Do not edit this file. Each theorem restates the matching `_aux` theorem in
`PrymParabolicRealizationProofs.lean`.

**Claimed (once the bodies are proved).** For a group `G` and a tuple `g` of length `r`, on the
explicit lifted complex `X̃(g)` of stage H3a (cells repeated in `PrymParabolicRealizationDefs`
under the prefix `hg2_`):
- the cellular boundaries compose to zero when `g₀ ⋯ g_{r−1} = 1`, over any commutative ring;
- the combinatorial monodromy of the cover `X̃(g)` over the Figure 1 complex: under product one,
  the lift from `b₀(x)` of the loop `ℓ_i = f_i f_{i+1}⁻¹` ends at `b₀(x g_i)`, and the edges
  `e_i` over `b₀ → p_i` meet every point over `p_i` exactly `ord(g_i)` times;
- for a finite group, a generating tuple and product one: the integral `2`-cycles are the
  multiples of the orientation chain `Σ_x Σ_i (A_i(x) − B_i(x))`, and cellular `H₁(X̃; ℤ)` is
  free of rank `r|G| + 2 − 2|G| − Σ_i |G/⟨g_i⟩|` (Riemann–Hurwitz);
- under product one, for any field `K`, the evaluation pairing identifies cellular `H¹(X̃; K)`
  with `Hom_ℤ(H₁(X̃; ℤ), K)` (universal coefficients);
- for the G32 root `b4b_root`, the B6-3b operator `Σ_h b4b_projectorCoeff h · h_*` on
  `H₁(X̃(b4b_root); ℤ)` has image of rank `12`.

The chain checks derive a `ℤ`-basis indexed by `Fin 12` of that image, the index type of
`b63d_lattice_rank`, and an abstract `ℤ`-linear isomorphism between the image and the B6-3
parameter lattice of any fibre satisfying the hypotheses of `b63d_lattice_rank`.

**Not claimed.** An embedding of the Figure 1 complex in the punctured sphere along the marked
root cover's loops; the identification of the combinatorial monodromy above with the based
monodromy of a cover of `b6t_punctured`; singular simplices lifting the cells; the comparison of
cellular and singular `H₁`; that the isomorphism with the B6-3 lattice is equivariant or
isometric. The statements are an implication from the stated combinatorial hypotheses only;
the tuple of the parameter-free statement is the repository's `b4b_root`, not identified with
the monodromy of the paper's base point `C₀`.
HC no distance; AV milestone no distance.
-/

